{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Creating output directory and handling JSON robustness**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_018fb13e2377dc3c016a94fc016d1c87d2ae2c8de59a887dd1\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Creating output directory and handling JSON robustness**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3armTEGrqAD2daIdZ8I4XGw8|fc_018fb13e2377dc3c016a94fc032a1c87d2b4089cb1e2a2620c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"OUT=/workspace/out; mkdir -p \"$OUT\"; cat > \"$OUT/module_map.json\" <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\", \"purpose\": \"CLI bootstrap: load settings, construct the repository, initialize the schema, and report readiness.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.config\", \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\", \"purpose\": \"Defines immutable Settings and maps environment variables to runtime configuration.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.models\", \"path\": \"minisvc/models.py\", \"purpose\": \"Defines the Order domain dataclass.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes\", \"path\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\", \"purpose\": \"Registers POST and GET order handlers on an HTTP adapter.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"path\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\", \"purpose\": \"Converts request payloads to Orders, persists or reads them, and builds response dictionaries.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"path\": \"minisvc/storage/repo.py\", \"purpose\": \"SQLite-backed OrderRepository for schema setup, inserts, and lookups.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.audit\", \"path\": \"minisvc/audit.py\", \"purpose\": \"Builds in-memory order event dictionaries; it does not persist audit records.\"}\n  ],\n  \"entry_points\": [\n    {\"id\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"kind\": \"console\", \"source\": \"pyproject.toml [project.scripts]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"kind\": \"API registration\", \"source\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\"},\n    {\"id\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"kind\": \"HTTP handler\", \"source\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\"},\n    {\"id\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"kind\": \"HTTP handler\", \"source\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\"}\n  ],\n  \"dependency_edges\": [\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"to\": \"minisvc.config\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"to\": \"environment\", \"type\": \"reads_config\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\", \"to\": \"SQLite database_path\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"}\n  ],\n  \"key_functions\": [\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"role\": \"Loads environment settings, creates OrderRepository, initializes orders table, and returns 0.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"role\": \"Reads MINISVC_DB (default orders.sqlite) and MINISVC_READONLY (only records a boolean).\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"role\": \"Binds POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id> callbacks.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"role\": \"Indexes required payload fields, casts total_cents to int, saves the Order, and returns a created response.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"role\": \"Looks up an order and returns either missing or serialized order data plus a read event.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"role\": \"Inserts one order with parameterized SQL in a SQLite transaction.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"role\": \"Queries one order by ID and reconstructs Order(*row).\"},\n    {\"name\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"role\": \"Returns an event dict; no database or file write occurs.\"}\n  ],\n  \"runtime_flows\": [\n    {\"name\": \"CLI startup\", \"steps\": [\"console script dispatches to minisvc.cli:main\", \"main passes os.environ to config.load_settings\", \"main instantiates OrderRepository(settings.database_path)\", \"repo.init_schema creates orders table if absent\", \"main prints readiness and returns 0\"]},\n    {\"name\": \"HTTP create-order\", \"steps\": [\"HTTP adapter invokes route callback registered by register_routes for POST /orders\", \"callback calls handlers.create_order(payload, repo)\", \"create_order constructs Order from order_id, customer, and int(total_cents)\", \"OrderRepository.save inserts the order into SQLite\", \"order_event creates an in-memory created event\", \"handler returns status, order_id, and event\"]}\n  ]\n}\nEOF\ncat > \"$OUT/architecture.md\" <<'EOF'\n# minisvc architecture\n\n## Modules\n\nThe active runtime is small and layered:\n\n- `minisvc.cli:main` is the console bootstrap declared in `pyproject.toml`. It loads config, builds `OrderRepository`, creates the schema, and prints readiness.\n- `minisvc.config` maps `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY` into frozen `Settings`.\n- `minisvc.models.Order` is the sole domain model.\n- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes` binds `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/<order_id>` to handlers.\n- `minisvc.api.handlers` validates only by direct field access and integer conversion, then calls the repository and event builder.\n- `minisvc.storage.repo.OrderRepository` owns SQLite schema, insert, and lookup operations.\n- `minisvc.audit:order_event` builds response data in memory.\n\n`minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package marker files, not business-logic modules.\n\n## Entry points and data flow\n\nThe executable entry point is `minisvc.cli:main`; the API integration point is `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`. On create, the adapter passes a payload to `create_order`, which constructs an `Order`, writes it through `OrderRepository.save`, and returns a dict with an event. Reads call `OrderRepository.get`, reconstruct an `Order`, and return its `__dict__` plus a read event.\n\n## Storage\n\nSQLite is selected by `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`. `init_schema` creates an `orders` table with a primary key and non-null customer and total. `save` uses parameterized SQL and a connection context manager; `get` opens a fresh connection per query. There is no audit table: `order_event` only returns a dict, and the event is not passed to storage.\n\n## Risks and extension points\n\n- `Settings.readonly` is never checked by CLI, routes, handlers, or repository, so writes still happen when `MINISVC_READONLY=1`.\n- There is no retry loop around SQLite writes, and duplicate IDs or database errors propagate.\n- Required payload fields are accessed directly; missing fields, invalid totals, oversized values, and unknown fields have no explicit policy.\n- The database path is environment-controlled and parent-directory creation, migrations, locking, and backup are unspecified.\n- Audit output is ephemeral and returned only in API responses; it is not durable or transactional with order writes.\n\nNatural extension points are a repository policy layer for readonly/retry behavior, explicit request validation at the handler boundary, and a durable audit repository with a transaction strategy.\nEOF\ncat > \"$OUT/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\" <<'EOF'\nclaim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"config.load_settings only stores readonly in Settings; cli.main and OrderRepository.save never inspect it\",\"contradicted\",\"A readonly deployment can still insert orders\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice\",\"README.md:7\",\"api.handlers.create_order calls repo.save once; storage.repo.OrderRepository.save has one sqlite execute and no retry loop\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures become immediate API errors\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"audit.order_event only returns a dict; storage.repo.init_schema creates only orders and no audit write exists\",\"contradicted\",\"Events can be lost and cannot support durable audit queries\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$OUT/risk_register.csv\" <<'EOF'\nrisk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:save and get use SQLite but there is no backup, migration, fsync, or parent-directory handling\",\"Data loss or startup failure in some deployment paths\",\"Define database lifecycle, migrations, backup/restore, and durable deployment storage\",\"storage owner\"\nR2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:order_event returns a dict; handlers.py returns it but repo.py has no audit table or insert\",\"No durable trail; audit is absent if a response is dropped\",\"Add an audit repository and transactionally persist order/action events\",\"security/compliance owner\"\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:load_settings reads MINISVC_DB and readonly, but readonly is unused\",\"Environment may claim read-only while writes remain enabled; relative DB path varies by cwd\",\"Enforce readonly before every write and validate/resolve configuration at startup\",\"runtime owner\"\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order directly indexes payload and calls int(total_cents)\",\"Malformed or unbounded input raises errors or creates invalid business data\",\"Add schema validation, bounds, field types, and consistent error responses\",\"API owner\"\nR5,write reliability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:OrderRepository.save executes once; no retry or conflict policy\",\"Transient locks and duplicate IDs fail without a defined client-safe response\",\"Add bounded retry for lock errors and explicit idempotency/conflict handling\",\"storage/API owners\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$OUT/onboarding_plan.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Onboarding plan\n\n## Read order\n\n1. Read `README.md` for stated behavior and its authority warning.\n2. Read `pyproject.toml` to find the `minisvc.cli:main` console entry point.\n3. Read `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/models.py` for settings and the data shape.\n4. Trace `minisvc/cli.py` into `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for startup and SQLite behavior.\n5. Trace `minisvc/api/routes.py` into `minisvc/api/handlers.py`, then `audit.py`.\n6. Skip `__init__.py` files except to note they are package markers; they contain no runtime business logic.\n\n## Run and test\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython -m minisvc.cli\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -c 'from minisvc.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())'\npython -m pytest\n```\n\nNo test suite is included in the fixture, so the last command may report that no tests were collected.\n\n## First trace point\n\nSet a breakpoint in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` line 6 (or log the payload there), then step into `OrderRepository.save` line 17. This shows input conversion, persistence, and where exceptions escape.\n\n## Safe first changes\n\n1. Add focused tests around `load_settings` defaults and `OrderRepository.get/save` using a temporary SQLite path; this does not alter production behavior.\n2. Add explicit payload validation in `create_order` with tests for missing fields and invalid `total_cents`, while preserving the current response contract for valid input.\n\nTreat readonly enforcement, retries, and durable audit storage as separate reviewed changes because the current implementation does not provide them.\nEOF\npython -m json.tool \"$OUT/module_map.json\" >/dev/null\nls -l \"$OUT\"","cwd":"/workspace"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":937,"output":3245,"cacheRead":16896,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":53,"totalTokens":21078,"cost":{"input":0.00018740000000000003,"output":0.003894,"cacheRead":0.00033792,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00441932}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788148736263,"responseId":"resp_018fb13e2377dc3c016a94fc00ac0887d280723b2e75da3ab0","rawStopReason":"completed"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3armTEGrqAD2daIdZ8I4XGw8|fc_018fb13e2377dc3c016a94fc032a1c87d2b4089cb1e2a2620c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/bin/bash: line 138: python: command not found\ntotal 24\n-rw-r--r--. 1 core dialout 2537 Aug 31 03:59 architecture.